virglrenderer: separable shaders redeclare the gl_PerVertex blocks they use

What: a shader of a separable program (TGSI PROPERTY SEPARABLE_PROGRAM, desktop GL)
redeclares its gl_PerVertex blocks. The vertex, tessellation evaluation and geometry
shaders always write "out gl_PerVertex { vec4 gl_Position; ... };", the tessellation
control shader "... } gl_out[];", and the tessellation and geometry shaders read through
"in gl_PerVertex { ... } gl_in[];". Members: gl_Position; gl_PointSize where the shader
writes (or reads) it; the clip and cull distance arrays the shader declared on their own
before, now inside the block; gl_ClipDistance[8] where the user clip planes are written.
Before, only a stage that was not the last one wrote the block, and only when its next
stage asked for it, which separable neighbours never do. Non-separable programs get the
same GLSL as before.
Why: GLSL 4.10 (ARB_separate_shader_objects) wants a separable shader to redeclare a
built-in block before it uses its members. Apple's GL (the software renderer and the GPU)
refuses to link it otherwise: "Built-in variable '<out gl_PerVertex.gl_Position>' must be
redeclared before use, with separate shader objects". Mesa's GL does not insist. The host
says VIRGL_CAP_V2_SSO (GL 4.1), so the guest's Mesa sends separable programs for apps that
use program pipelines (glCreateShaderProgramv, GL_PROGRAM_SEPARABLE): every one was refused
and its draws skipped (virgl-shader-failure-skip-draws.patch), #567. A loose
gl_ClipDistance beside a redeclared block crashes Apple's GLSL compiler (glpCGAssign), so
the arrays go into the block, never beside it.
Upstream: the same conditions in virglrenderer main (checked 2026-10-28); not sent.
Test: Tests/virgl/test-separable-pervertex.c: separable pipelines on Apple's software
renderer (vertex + fragment with a varying, gl_PointSize, + geometry, + tessellation,
+ tessellation + geometry; blocks that differ between stages, gl_in[].gl_PointSize, clip
distance arrays inside the blocks, a flat integer varying, transform feedback, separable
and whole stages linked as one program) draw their colour and nothing is refused; each
row fails without this patch. Tests/virgl/test-sysval-block.c's separable rows now run on
these blocks (its GL stand-in that added the block is gone).
Not fixed here (other IO of separable programs, upstream code): Apple's GL refuses a
layout location on a patch variable, which vrend gives every separable patch varying, and
vrend puts a separable varying array at location 31 - its first, past the last location.
virgl-shader-separable-patch-varyings.patch and virgl-shader-separable-varying-arrays.patch
fix both (#589); arrays in a geometry or tessellation shader's block are still refused (rows
in the same test).

